<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Jan palm oil output seen down 9.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Jan palm oil output seen down 9.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's palm oil output in January is estimated to fall 9.0 percent from December's 637,865 tonnes, crop forecaster Ivan Wong said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Wong has projected palm oil exports in January at 545,000 tonnes and stocks at the end of January at 730,000 tonnes.  </p>
<p>The Palm Oil Registration and Licensing Authority put exports in December at 637,899 tonnes and end-December stocks at 792,687 tonnes.</p>
<p>Wong said in a report that output in eastern Sabah and Sarawak states in the last two weeks had been affected by a resumption of monsoon rains.</p>
<p>&quot;If the rains are prolonged, a double-digit decline could not be ruled out,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>Malaysia palm oil supply-demand estimate/projection as of January 21, 1997. (All figures in '000 tonnes)</p>
<p>			    Dec	 Jan	 Feb	  Mar</p>
<p>Opening stocks	  604	 435	 380-385    295-300</p>
<p>Imports		   -	   -	   -	    -</p>
<p>Production		638	 580-585   450-455    645-650</p>
<p>TTL supply	     1242	1015-1020  830-840    940-950</p>
<p>Exports		    22	   1	   3	     3</p>
<p>Domestic use	    784	 630-635   530-535    630-635</p>
<p>TTL offtake	     806	 631-636   533-538    633-638</p>
<p>Endmonth CPO stocks   435	 380-385   295-300    305-310</p>
<p>Endmonth PPO stocks   357	 345-350   335-340    315-320</p>
<p>TTL PO stocks	   793	 725-735   630-640    620-630</p>
<p>PPO exports	     616	 540-545   470-475    570-575</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 7510)</p>
